import QtslAux.QuantumStackVonNeumann

/-! # Descent for nets of von Neumann algebras: essential surjectivity from a common implementer

`QtslAux.QuantumStackVonNeumann` proved the descent comparison for a net
of von Neumann algebras fully faithful under generation and
connectivity, and `QtslAux.QuantumStackNormality` showed why no
unconditional essential-surjectivity clause can hold in the directed
regime: local normality does not imply global normality, and no
completeness of the fibre categories can manufacture the missing global
object.  What survives at operator grade is the **certified** form of
the clause: a descent datum together with a separately checkable
witness whose *promotion* to the global object is the theorem — the
hypothesis carries a certificate, and generation upgrades the
certificate, rather than the conclusion being assumed.

At the standard-representation fragment the natural certificate is a
**common implementer**: a single star projection `p` commuting with
every member algebra of the sieve, to whose memberwise restrictions the
descent datum is coherently isomorphic.  This module proves that clause:

* **The certificate, packaged** (`implementerDatum`): the memberwise
  restrictions of a common implementer form a lawful descent datum —
  every component is `p` in the commutant of its member algebra, every
  gluing morphism has underlying operator literally `p`, and the
  cocycle condition is idempotence.  The datum is definable *below*
  generation: only memberwise commutation is consumed.

* **The promotion** (`implementer_mem_commutant`): if the global
  algebra lies in the von Neumann algebra generated by the member
  algebras, an operator commuting with every member algebra commutes
  with the global algebra — the bicommutant lemma
  (`VonNeumannAlgebra.commute_all_of_forall_commute`) applied to the
  union.  Generation is consumed here and only here.  The promoted
  witness is a global subrepresentation (`implementerSubRep`).

* **Essential surjectivity from the certificate**
  (`descentComparisonW_essImage_of_commonImplementer`): any descent
  datum isomorphic to the implementer datum lies in the essential image
  of the comparison functor.  "Coherently isomorphic on every member"
  is an isomorphism in the category of descent data — the
  compatibility field of a morphism of descent data *is* the coherence
  of the memberwise family; a bare memberwise family of isomorphisms
  would be strictly weaker and would not suffice.

* **No connectivity is consumed.**  Fullness needed the members
  zigzag-connected to tie the components of a descent morphism to one
  operator; here the certificate itself supplies the one operator, so
  the object clause holds over an arbitrary sieve.  No operator
  topology appears anywhere in this file, as in the parent module.

The witness `constWNet_implementerDatum_in_essImage` instantiates the
clause on the canonical interior cover of the landed Minkowski site.
As at the fully-faithful clause, genuinely non-attained
(directed-regime) instances require infinite-dimensional nets beyond
current mathlib vocabulary — which is exactly why the certificate — not
attainment, and not an unconditional gluing axiom — is the honest
hypothesis.

Descent for categories fibered over sites is Benini–Grant-Stuart–Schenkel
(arXiv:2404.14510); nets of operator algebras on causal diamonds are
Haag–Kastler (J. Math. Phys. 5, 848 (1964)); complete W*-categories are
Henriques–Nivedita–Penneys (arXiv:2411.01678).
-/

noncomputable section

namespace Qtsl
namespace QuantumStack

open CategoryTheory DiamondSite QuantumDescent

variable {X : Type*} [PartialOrder X]
variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]
  [CompleteSpace H]
variable {N : WNet X H} {D : Diamond X} {S : Sieve D}

/-! ## The certificate: a common implementer -/

/-- A member algebra's element lies in the union of the member
algebras. -/
theorem mem_netUnion_of_member {E : Diamond X} (h : E ≤ D)
    (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE h)) {x : H →L[ℂ] H} (hx : x ∈ N.alg E) :
    x ∈ netUnion N D S := by
  simp only [netUnion, Set.mem_iUnion]
  exact ⟨E, h, hS, hx⟩

/-- An operator commuting with the union of the member algebras lies in
the commutant of every member algebra. -/
theorem implementer_mem_commutant_member {p : H →L[ℂ] H}
    (hcomm : ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * p = p * x)
    {E : Diamond X} (h : E ≤ D) (hS : S.arrows (homOfLE h)) :
    p ∈ (N.alg E).commutant := by
  rw [VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_commutant_iff]
  intro g hg
  exact hcomm g (mem_netUnion_of_member h hS hg)

/-- **The implementer datum**: the memberwise restrictions of a common
implementer — one star projection commuting with every member algebra —
form a descent datum.  Every gluing morphism has underlying operator
`p` itself, and the cocycle condition is idempotence.  Only memberwise
commutation is consumed: the certificate exists below generation. -/
@[reducible] def implementerDatum (N : WNet X H) (D : Diamond X)
    (S : Sieve D) (p : H →L[ℂ] H) (hp : IsStarProjection p)
    (hcomm : ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * p = p * x) :
    WDescentDatum N D S where
  obj := fun _ h hS => ⟨p, hp, implementer_mem_commutant_member hcomm h hS⟩
  glue := fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE =>
    { hom := ⟨p, implementer_mem_commutant_member hcomm (hEF.trans hFD) hSE,
        by rw [hp.isIdempotentElem.eq, hp.isIdempotentElem.eq]⟩
      inv := ⟨p, implementer_mem_commutant_member hcomm (hEF.trans hFD) hSE,
        by rw [hp.isIdempotentElem.eq, hp.isIdempotentElem.eq]⟩
      hom_inv_id := SubRep.Hom.ext hp.isIdempotentElem.eq
      inv_hom_id := SubRep.Hom.ext hp.isIdempotentElem.eq }
  cocycle := fun _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => hp.isIdempotentElem.eq

/-! ## The promotion: generation upgrades the certificate -/

/-- **The promotion lemma.**  If the global algebra lies in the von
Neumann algebra generated by the member algebras, an operator commuting
with every member algebra lies in the commutant of the *global*
algebra: the bicommutant lemma applied to the star-closed union.  This
is the single consumption site of the generation hypothesis — the
certificate is promoted, not assumed. -/
theorem implementer_mem_commutant (N : WNet X H) {D : Diamond X}
    {S : Sieve D}
    (hgen : N.alg D ≤ VonNeumannAlgebra.generate (netUnion N D S))
    {p : H →L[ℂ] H} (hcomm : ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * p = p * x) :
    p ∈ (N.alg D).commutant := by
  rw [VonNeumannAlgebra.mem_commutant_iff]
  intro g hg
  exact VonNeumannAlgebra.commute_all_of_forall_commute
    (netUnion_star_closed N D S) hcomm (hgen hg)

/-- The promoted certificate: a common implementer is a
subrepresentation of the global algebra. -/
@[reducible] def implementerSubRep (N : WNet X H) {D : Diamond X}
    {S : Sieve D}
    (hgen : N.alg D ≤ VonNeumannAlgebra.generate (netUnion N D S))
    {p : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : IsStarProjection p)
    (hcomm : ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * p = p * x) :
    SubRep (N.alg D) :=
  ⟨p, hp, implementer_mem_commutant N hgen hcomm⟩

/-- The comparison functor sends the promoted certificate to the
implementer datum, up to isomorphism of descent data: every underlying
operator on both sides is `p`, and the compatibility squares are
definitional against the comparison's tautological gluing. -/
@[reducible] def implementerComparisonIso (N : WNet X H) {D : Diamond X}
    {S : Sieve D}
    (hgen : N.alg D ≤ VonNeumannAlgebra.generate (netUnion N D S))
    {p : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : IsStarProjection p)
    (hcomm : ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * p = p * x) :
    (descentComparisonW N D S).obj (implementerSubRep N hgen hp hcomm)
      ≅ implementerDatum N D S p hp hcomm where
  hom :=
    { app := fun _ h hS =>
        ⟨p, implementer_mem_commutant_member hcomm h hS,
          by rw [hp.isIdempotentElem.eq, hp.isIdempotentElem.eq]⟩
      compat := fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE => rfl }
  inv :=
    { app := fun _ h hS =>
        ⟨p, implementer_mem_commutant_member hcomm h hS,
          by rw [hp.isIdempotentElem.eq, hp.isIdempotentElem.eq]⟩
      compat := fun {E F} hEF hFD hSF hSE => rfl }
  hom_inv_id := WDescentDatum.Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS =>
    SubRep.Hom.ext hp.isIdempotentElem.eq)
  inv_hom_id := WDescentDatum.Hom.ext' (fun _ hE hS =>
    SubRep.Hom.ext hp.isIdempotentElem.eq)

/-! ## Essential surjectivity from the certificate -/

/-- The implementer datum lies in the essential image of the
comparison: the promoted certificate glues it. -/
theorem implementerDatum_in_essImage (N : WNet X H) {D : Diamond X}
    {S : Sieve D}
    (hgen : N.alg D ≤ VonNeumannAlgebra.generate (netUnion N D S))
    {p : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : IsStarProjection p)
    (hcomm : ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * p = p * x) :
    ∃ ρ : SubRep (N.alg D),
      Nonempty ((descentComparisonW N D S).obj ρ
        ≅ implementerDatum N D S p hp hcomm) :=
  ⟨implementerSubRep N hgen hp hcomm,
    ⟨implementerComparisonIso N hgen hp hcomm⟩⟩

/-- **Essential surjectivity from a common implementer.**  Any descent
datum coherently isomorphic on every member of the sieve to the
restrictions of one star projection commuting with every member algebra
lies in the essential image of the descent comparison, provided the
global algebra lies in the von Neumann algebra generated by the member
algebras.  Generation *promotes* the certificate to the global object
(`implementer_mem_commutant`) rather than assuming the conclusion; the
coherence of the memberwise identification is the isomorphism of
descent data itself.  No connectivity hypothesis appears: the
certificate supplies the one operator that connectivity supplied for
the morphism clause. -/
theorem descentComparisonW_essImage_of_commonImplementer (N : WNet X H)
    {D : Diamond X} {S : Sieve D}
    (hgen : N.alg D ≤ VonNeumannAlgebra.generate (netUnion N D S))
    {p : H →L[ℂ] H} (hp : IsStarProjection p)
    (hcomm : ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * p = p * x)
    (Xd : WDescentDatum N D S)
    (e : Nonempty (Xd ≅ implementerDatum N D S p hp hcomm)) :
    ∃ ρ : SubRep (N.alg D),
      Nonempty ((descentComparisonW N D S).obj ρ ≅ Xd) := by
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := e
  exact ⟨implementerSubRep N hgen hp hcomm,
    ⟨(implementerComparisonIso N hgen hp hcomm).trans e.symm⟩⟩

/-! ## Witness

The unit implementer on the constant net at the canonical interior
cover of the landed Minkowski site: the hypotheses of the theorem are
jointly satisfiable.  Generation holds by attainment here, as at the
fully-faithful witness; genuinely non-attained instances require
infinite-dimensional nets beyond current mathlib vocabulary. -/

/-- The identity is a common implementer for any net and any sieve. -/
theorem one_commutes (N : WNet X H) (D : Diamond X) (S : Sieve D) :
    ∀ x ∈ netUnion N D S, x * (1 : H →L[ℂ] H) = 1 * x :=
  fun _ _ => by rw [mul_one, one_mul]

/-- Non-vacuity: the unit implementer datum of the constant net on the
standard diamond of the Minkowski site is glued by the promoted
certificate. -/
theorem constWNet_implementerDatum_in_essImage :
    ∃ ρ : SubRep ((constWNet (Mink ℝ) H).alg Dstar),
      Nonempty ((descentComparisonW (constWNet (Mink ℝ) H) Dstar
          (interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit) Dstar)).obj ρ
        ≅ implementerDatum (constWNet (Mink ℝ) H) Dstar
            (interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit) Dstar)
            1 (IsStarProjection.one _)
            (one_commutes (constWNet (Mink ℝ) H) Dstar
              (interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit) Dstar))) :=
  implementerDatum_in_essImage (constWNet (Mink ℝ) H)
    (S := interiorSieve ((minkowskiKit (E := ℝ)).toMixingKit) Dstar)
    (le_generate_of_attained (MixingKit.sub_of_interiorMem E₃_interior)
      ⟨E₃, E₃_interior, le_rfl⟩ le_rfl)
    (IsStarProjection.one _)
    (one_commutes _ _ _)

end QuantumStack
end Qtsl
